      {
        "concept": "Using cumulative frequency graphs to find data frequencies",
        "explanation": "By reading values from the graph at specific points, you can find the number of values less than or greater than that point."
      },
      {
        "concept": "Interpreting the shape of cumulative frequency graphs",
        "explanation": "The steepness of the graph segments indicates concentration of data values in that range."
      },
      {
        "concept": "Estimating median, quartiles, and interquartile range",
        "explanation": "Median and quartiles can be estimated by locating the 50%, 25%, and 75% cumulative frequencies and reading corresponding values on the horizontal axis."
